  "identifier": "gow-ragnarok-story-chart-2026",
  "headline": "God of War Ragnarok Story Chart: The Path (18 main missions) plus the best detour windows",
  "description": "A clear main-story map (The Path) and a chapter-level plan for when to detour for upgrades, exploration, and side content without breaking pacing.",
  "articleBody": "Note: This page includes main-mission titles.\n\n1. The Path: all 18 main missions\n1) Surviving Fimbulwinter\n2) The Quest for Tyr\n3) Old Friends\n4) Groa’s Secret\n5) The Lost Sanctuary\n6) The Reckoning\n7) The Runaway\n8) Into the Fire\n9) The Word of Fate\n10) Forging Destiny\n11) Unleashing Hel\n12) Reunion\n13) Creatures of Prophecy\n14) Unlocking the Mask\n15) Hunting for Solace\n16) The Summoning\n17) The Realms at War\n18) Beyond Ragnarok\n\n2. Detour windows (a stability-first pacing plan)\n- Between missions 2–4: learn exploration patterns, prioritize upgrade materials and reliable runics.\n- Around mission 6 (Vanaheim): once the River Delta opens, it’s worth grabbing a strong midgame armor foundation.\n- Missions 9–10: difficulty spikes are often level gaps, so upgrade weapons/armor before you feel stuck.\n- After mission 13: Vanaheim opens further, improving upgrade-material efficiency.\n- Before mission 17: if you want endgame builds (e.g., Berserker pieces), use this as a clean breakpoint.\n- After mission 18: postgame routes (collectibles, optional bosses, 100% completion) become the main focus.\n\nUse this story chart as the backbone. The chapter-by-chapter skill and gear recommendations live in separate pages.",
